{
  "Scenes.Boat.BoatExplore.MuddyFaintOdor": "[if (ismer) {it|The water}] appears somewhat muddy and has a faint pungent odor. "
  "Scenes.Boat.BoatExplore.NeedsPurifying": "knowing what's been pumped into it for years, Marae needs time to purify it all. "
  "Scenes.Boat.BoatExplore.ReachDockBoard": "You reach the dock without any incident and board the small rowboat. The water is calm and placid, [if (ismer) {inviting you for a swim, but|perfect for rowing.}] "
  "Scenes.Boat.BoatExplore.SmellsLikeSex": "You realize what it smells like--sex. "
  "Scenes.Boat.BoatExplore.ToxicWaterNote": "there's something faintly toxic about it."
  "Scenes.Boat.DiscoverBoat.BoatAddedToPlaces": "<b>(\"Boat\" added to Places menu.)</b>"
  "Scenes.Boat.DiscoverBoat.LakeJourneyFindBoat": "As you journey around the lake, the air is fresh, and the grass is cool and soft under your feet. Soft waves lap against the muddy sand of the lake-shore, as if radiating outward from the lake. You pass around a few bushes carefully, being wary of hidden 'surprises', and come upon a small dock. The dock is crafted from old growth trees lashed together with some crude rope. Judging by the appearance of the rope, it is very old and has not been seen to in quite some time. Tied to the dock is a small rowboat, only about seven feet long and three feet wide. The boat seems to be in much better condition than the dock--it actually looks rather new. You're confident it'll allow you to make trips onto the lake.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Boat.FindLightRailAvenger.ArmsBurnRowing": "You're near the center of the lake. Your arms are burning with exhaustion, and it's becoming evident that there's nothing interesting to be found here."
  "Scenes.Boat.FindLightRailAvenger.DeepUnderwaterObject": "[pg]The object is hidden pretty deep underwater, but, for some reason, you don't feel shortness of breath. You've been underwater for several dozen seconds now, but you're absolutely fine. Staring at the reflection gives you breath and energizes you."
  "Scenes.Boat.FindLightRailAvenger.DiveDownDecision": "[pg]You decide to dive down and see what it is."
  "Scenes.Boat.FindLightRailAvenger.GlintUnderBoat": "[pg]Suddenly, a glint at the bottom of the lake catches your eyes."
  "Scenes.Boat.FindLightRailAvenger.InvestigateGlint": "[pg]You move in to investigate. It is a rather curious thing; the clouds have congregated in a way that the only ray of sunshine is beaming down onto the submerged metallic object. Its reflection is fierce, almost as bright as the sun itself."
  "Scenes.Boat.FindLightRailAvenger.RetrieveSword": "[pg]You finally reach the object, and it's a sword, and a sheath nearby! It is stabbed deep on a rock, but you manage to pull it off with remarkable ease. You head back to the surface to better analyze your prize."
  "Scenes.Boat.FindLightRailAvenger2.DullEdgeless": "[pg]You thumb at the sword's edge to check its sharpness, and, to your surprise, it is absolutely dull. You attempt to cut anything nearby, from wood to cloth to a strand of hair, but nothing works. What a lousy sword! Well, it may sell as decoration."
  "Scenes.Boat.FindLightRailAvenger2.KatanaDescription": "[pg]It's a katana, with a matching wood sheath. The metal on the blade is marvelous, and the metal was forged in a way that resulted in a wavy pattern resembling a dragon throughout its length. The sheath is black, with exquisite red and gold drawings of dragons, and a red ribbon at its tip."
  "Scenes.Boat.FindLightRailAvenger2.SurfaceOnBoat": "You surface and climb on your boat. You then look at the sword."
  "Scenes.Boat.GoRowOnTheBoat.RowOutWondering": "[pg]You set out, wondering if you'll find any strange islands or creatures in the lake.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Boat.GoRowOnTheBoat.WarySetOut": "[pg]Wary, you set out in the comfort of the boat, only submerging the end of your tail in the water, and wondering if you'll find any strange islands or creatures in the lake.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Boat.NothingSpecial.YouRowForNearly": "{0}"
  "Scenes.Boat.TakeSword.TakeSwordDecoration": "Well, it would make for a pretty decent decoration for your camp. You take the sword, a bit disappointed with the result of your exploration."
}
